  "sourceUse": "The formal 2026–2027 regulations define four variants. The generic target has no variant, so the PThU trajectory with Greek illustrates the breadth of theological disciplines and both biblical languages. The university programme page identifies it as the most selected variant. The PThU route uses Practical Theology in year one, Psychology and Sociology of Religion and Dogmatics in year two, and the 30 EC specified PThU block in year three. The remaining year-three credit includes one 7.5 EC specialisation, 7.5 EC seminar, 5 EC science communication and 10 EC thesis. Origins of Religion is the first listed specialisation in Article 7.1, independent of UCR fit. Mentoring and introduction are uncredited.",
  "progression": {
    "firstYear": "Hebrew 1 and Hebrew Bible and Ancient Judaism are in 1b. Hebrew 2 is in 2a, following Hebrew 1. The 2b Old Testament Exegesis exam requires Hebrew 2 and Hebrew Bible and Ancient Judaism under Art. 9.3. The Ocasys exegesis entry repeats only the Hebrew 2 condition.",
    "secondYear": "A minimum of 45 first-year EC plus named prerequisites permits year-two units. Greek I and New Testament are in 1a, Greek II in 1b, and New Testament Exegesis in 2a. Article 9.3 uses New Testament: Text and Cultural Context; the dated grid labels the current New Testament course as THB2-NT, and the dated course covers the text and its contexts. Greek II also precedes the exegesis assessment.",
    "thirdYear": "Year-three entry normally requires completing year one and satisfying named prerequisites. Historical Theology requires Theology: Concepts and Methods, Turning Points in Christian Thought and Dogmatics under the controlling Article 9.3. The catalogue description calls the historical course Christianity from Reformation until the Present. The adopted rule and dated grid explicitly name the current Turning Points unit, whose coverage focuses on post-1500 thinkers. Dogmatics is also required for Intercultural Theology and appears in year two 2b, before both courses. The specialisation and thesis seminar are in 2a.",
    "thesis": "Article 9.3 and the dated thesis entry require 60 EC of second- and third-year units before the thesis. A completed second year satisfies the credit threshold. The seminar is in 2a before the 10 EC thesis in 2b."
  }
}
